assette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in largest dimension are encountered in the axillary fat and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   No lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large bisected lymph nodes  one lymph node per cassette  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Less than 10  of tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unknown.
