Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Miriam D Post  M D  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Amendment  1  Corrected Transcription Error not in Final Diagnosis Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the left breast  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on nine  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 immunostained levels  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ASSOCIATED WITH A DENSE LYMPHOPLASMACYTIC INFILTRATE  SEE TABLE AND NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE   NOTE  The presence of solid nests of cells with high nuclear grade and a diffuse  dense lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate prompts consideration of medullary carcinoma  However  while superficially the tumor appears histologically well circumscribed  scattered residual non neoplastic lobules are present within the main body of the tumor  which is not compatible with medullary carcinoma  This feature is highlighted by immunohistochemical stains for p63 and myosin  which also confirm that the vast majority of the nests of tumor cells are invasive  with only a few scattered foci of ductal carcinoma in situ  A minority of the tumor shows a more conventional infiltrative growth pattern  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  hot and blue   are two lymph nodes connected by a thin septae of fat  The larger node is separated from the smaller node  The larger node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The smaller node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The smaller node is inked black  The larger node is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The smaller node is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm breast specimen  The posterior surface is inked black and the anterior inked blue  The superior surface is inked green and the inferior inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm circular firm tan white nodular mass  The margins are as follows  0 8cm to the deep margin  0 8cm to the anterior margin  1 0cm to the superior margin  1 0cm to the inferior margin  1 7cm to the medial margin  and 2 0cm to the lateral margin  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass in relation to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass in relation to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section mass from the medial end   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from center of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from medial 