n  Called to OR by Dr  Yeh   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received in formalin in a single container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   patient s name and medical record number  It consists of a double wire  localized excisional breast biopsy which has been six inked by the surgeon   The specimen measures 11 0cm from lateral to medial  6 1cm from anterior to  posterior  and 2 9cm from superior to inferior  Two wires are present within  the specimen  Wire  1 enters the specimen at the anteroinferior margin  1 4cm  from the medial margin  0 9cm from the superior margin  and 2 3cm from the  lateral margin  Wire  2 courses superficially along the anterior aspect of the  specimen from lateral to medial  approximately equidistant from the superior  and inferior margins  This wire is dislodged during processing of the  specimen  Three sutures are present in the specimen  a short suture marks the  superior aspect of the specimen  a long suture marks the lateral aspect  and a  whip stitch marks the posterior aspect  per surgeon  the chest wall margin    The specimen has been radiographed by the surgeon and orientation of the  specimen is correlated with the radiograph  Based on this correlation  the  clip is located nearest to the medial margin and the calcifications present in  the radiograph are located posteromedially  The specimen is serially sectioned  from medial to lateral into 10 slices  slice  1 represents the medial margin    slice  10 the lateral margin   In slice  2  there is a red brown hemorrhagic  area clip which may represent the core biopsy site  This is located 1 1cm  from the superior  0 8cm from the medial  2 9cm from the posterior  2 2cm  from the anterior  10 2cm from the lateral  and 0 7cm from the inferior  margin  A firm  tan nodule is present in slices  3 and  4  located at the  medial margin  1 4cm from the superior margin  1 8cm from the inferior  margin  3 8cm from the posterior margin  7 0cm from the lateral margin  and  2 0cm from the anterior margin  Areas of possible calcifications are located  in slices  1 through  4  These slices are entirely submitted for microscopic  examination  The specimen has been discussed with Dr  Richardson   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible core biopsy site and superior and medial margins  2 frags   RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible core biopsy site and medial margin  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in slice  3 and medial margin  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in slice  3 and superior and medial margins  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in slice  4 and medial and inferior margins  1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of nodule  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slices  1 through  4  lateral to medial  multi frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central fibrous tissue in slice  8  1 frag  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional posterior margin  multi frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior margin  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  2 frags  RSS   SBL lp  CASE NUMBER  BS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  8 8  REMOVED_CASE_ID    report_end  , Positive.
