inely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm portion of unremarkable breast tissue  No discrete lesions are identified  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a total right mastectomy specimen  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm right breast with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm tan unremarkable skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ill defined  firm to hard gray mass  0 2cm from the superior resection margin adjacent to the skin ellipse and 3 0cm from the deep margin  A portion of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  2 and frozen section  3  and submitted respectively in cassettes C and D  further sectioning of the mass reveals focally hemorrhagic portions  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of dense white fibrous connective tissue  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of irregular adipose tissue from which two tan pink firm lymph nodes are identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Section Code  E F  mass with closest superior margin  G I  remainder of mass  J L  irregular pink white fibrous areas  M  axillary lymph n