in mass   and numerous enlarged lymph nodes were present in the left axilla  largest 3  cm   A core needle biopsy revealed a moderately differentiated invasive  carcinoma with ductal and lobular features that was positive for ER and PR and  negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  reviewed as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The patient underwent neoadjuvant chemotherapy  The main mass decreased in  size to 1 5cm with regression of the linear clumped enhancement  The lymph  nodes were no longer enlarged   In the mastectomy there was a firm fibrous area  6 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm   in the upper  to middle outer left breast  Fibrotic areas were present extending laterally   4 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm   and medially  5 x 3 x 2 0cm   from this mass over a total  area of REMOVED_DATE x 6 7cm  A tumor bed is identified in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  taken from the  lower outer quadrant  discrete area not seen on gross examination  and measures  1 2cm on the slide with an overall cellularity of 5   When compared to the  pre treatment core biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the tumor bed shows an approximately  50  reduction in cellularity  corresponding to a Miller Payne grade 3 response   In the remainder of the 8 6cm area  residual invasive carcinoma is present as  multiple foci  up to 0 5cm   associated with extensive lymphovascular invasion   Evidence of treatment effect is not seen in this area  An additional 0 2cm  invasive carcinoma is identified outside of this area within the representative  sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    and this focus is associated with  lymphovascular invasion   The residual carcinoma in the breast and lymph nodes appears viable   The residual cancer burden score based on the post treatment tumor bed size of  1 5 x 1 5cm with 5  cellularity is REMOVED_DATE  RCB II    This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC y  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID c  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    RIGHT BREAST  PROPHYLACTIC SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   Dense fibrous 